Magicbane's magic properties at +2 are very good; not so much the probes,
but the stuns, the confusion, the cancellation, and their combined effects.
It was very effective even in the games where I wielded Magicbane as my
exclusive primary weapon.

But opinions differ. (And there had been rough discussions in the past.)

If you want to hit single monsters in melee, a +7 is likely better. But
there are other choices; throwing missiles before you are in melee range,
or circumvent the one (or the few) monsters. If you are surrounded by a
lot of creatures melee is also not always the best choice; engrave the
E-word, use conflict, break a wand of teleport (or any other appropriate
wands), teleport or level teleport yourself, etc. If some magic attack of
Magicbane is successful on one of the monsters you may leave it alive and
concentrate on the next one. Even if you cannot evade the melee, a +2
artifact weapon is not a table knife; while not the best in damage, it
is still quite good. And cancelling a spellcaster, for example, can be
quite handy. You may also carry a second highly enchanted artifact with
you and switch weapon if you like. There are so many possibilities...

So it surely depends. ;-)

